#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""frame-snip: screenshot a rectangle of the window you're using, then copy it, save it, copy
its text (OCR), or read its text aloud (Narrate).

  frame-snip            capture the window the Steam session has focused (the desktop, or a
                        window you floated) and open the selection window
  frame-snip FILE       select from an image file instead (for testing)
  frame-snip --narrate IMAGE TEXT   (internal) the narration panel: reads TEXT aloud beside IMAGE

Drag a rectangle with the laser (or mouse), then pick an action. Esc or right-click cancels.
The selection window opens on the Steam session's display, so it shows up as a VR window.
Tools: Tesseract (OCR, Homebrew), Piper (speech, offline), wl-copy (clipboard; the Shared
clipboard tweak carries it to VR windows).
"""
